Subject: kernel memory/CPU hot-plug, and a udev rule that onlines added CPUs

docker-machine-ctl resize grows the running VM through VMware's hot-add (VixVM_HotPlugMemory,
VixVM_HotPlugCPU), which Fusion applies by a hard suspend-and-resume. The guest needs the kernel to
take the ACPI hot-add notifications: memory then comes online by itself
(MEMORY_HOTPLUG_DEFAULT_ONLINE), and an added CPU arrives offline, so a udev rule onlines it. The
rule's file is also ctl's marker that the VM booted a kernel that can take a hot-add (spike,
2026-11-24). PSI (/proc/pressure) is what self-sizing reads to tell the VM is short of memory or CPU.
diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
index d0a50b3..230c9f3 100644
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -449,6 +449,7 @@ RUN { \
 	rm -v etc/sysconfig/ntpserver
 
 COPY files/forgiving-getty files/shutdown ./usr/local/sbin/
+COPY files/udev/99-mavergreen-cpu-online.rules ./etc/udev/rules.d/
 
 # getty/inittab setup
 RUN awk -F: ' \
diff --git a/files/kernel-config.d/mavergreen-hotplug b/files/kernel-config.d/mavergreen-hotplug
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bca21bc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/files/kernel-config.d/mavergreen-hotplug
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+CONFIG_MEMORY_HOTPLUG=y
+CONFIG_MEMORY_HOTPLUG_DEFAULT_ONLINE=y
+CONFIG_ACPI_HOTPLUG_MEMORY=y
+CONFIG_ACPI_HOTPLUG_CPU=y
+CONFIG_PSI=y
diff --git a/files/udev/99-mavergreen-cpu-online.rules b/files/udev/99-mavergreen-cpu-online.rules
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..59ecbfe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/files/udev/99-mavergreen-cpu-online.rules
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+# Mavergreen Container Tools: bring a CPU that VMware hot-adds to the running VM online.
+SUBSYSTEM=="cpu", ACTION=="add", ATTR{online}="1"
